node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated protobuf code (cpp, python, ts) — machine-specific, not committed.
#
# buf.gen.yaml's cpp and python plugins are `protoc_builtin`: buf has no
# embedded compiler for those, so it shells out to whatever protoc is on PATH,
# and the output carries a hard version assert against that protoc's runtime
# (the #error block at the top of any .pb.h). Committing it meant every dev
# box and CI runner with a different protobuf package produced a spurious diff.
# Generate it instead: `buf generate` here, or scripts/install_harness.sh.
gen/
